WEBVTT

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:09.150
Ninety-six, ninety-seven,
ninety-eight, ninety-nine...

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.330
Okay...

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:34.130
I don't like this kind of weather.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:55.860
Tell me, tell me, what color is in season now?

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:57.160
Smiling white

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:58.570
Tearful blue

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:01.200
Let's mix them together and find out

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:06.540
Today is sunny, so take out your canvas

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:09.290
Have some ice cream and lemon soda

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:11.960
Then draw some exciting and colorful toppings

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:16.010
Hey, rough sketch, please

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:21.890
Let's do a self portrait contest

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:24.680
Yuno

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:29.150
All right! Don't get grouchy later

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:27.900
Miyako

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:30.400
Hiro

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:36.240
When the switch is flipped, I go wa-ha-ha

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:33.650
Sae

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:42.580
l hope everyone is having a great time

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:44.120
The race is on

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:46.910
I've gotta finish my apple quickly

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:49.540
No, that's not for eating

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:53.210
Let's take it easy

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:58.130
Fruits are our display models

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:02.970
So start drawing

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:05.850
It's our homework

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:13.270
October 12th: Stormy Drying Agent

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:22.200
Blessed with nice weather, it is a marvelous
day to have a sports festival.

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:27.000
Remember sports are just as
important as studying.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.250
Work just as hard as you do any other day.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.590
Let's take a break until the rain stops.

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:50.020
What's the size?

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:52.520
Eh? Mine is nine.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.360
I was talking about the typhoon.

00:02:58.990 --> 00:03:00.240
Hello!

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.860
It started raining.

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:06.410
I wonder if it can be done tomorrow?

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:10.870
I hate it when the plan is up in the air.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:17.250
We should have a dome,
so they won't need to cancel.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:19.210
A dome?

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:23.760
But then what would be the use of the gym?

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:28.060
The gym floor is good,
the dome is on the ground.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.560
Oh, I see, if so...

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:33.020
That will never happen.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:39.610
We're not going to be called yet, are we?
I need to use the restroom.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:42.280
It's probably okay. Just go.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:44.070
Okay.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.340
Ki-Kintaro!

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:06.090
What?

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:10.060
Well, um, I saw it just a moment
ago over there.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:12.310
Yunocchi, did you finish your business?

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:14.730
Oh, that's right. See you later.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:19.980
The rain seems to have stopped,
so we are resuming.

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:22.650
Yuno! Hurry up.

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:24.110
Okay!

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:40.460
I'm afraid our white team is going to win again.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.090
Natsume?

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:47.010
After all, the white team has won
for five years in a row.

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:53.810
Who was that?

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:55.640
She's from class B.

00:04:55.640 --> 00:05:00.400
Damn, if I had been able to participate last year,
I'm sure the red team would have won.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:03.990
Why couldn't you participate last year?

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:05.570
I had the mumps.

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:07.200
At your age?!

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:11.910
Hurry and line up.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:18.420
Broadcast Club

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:18.420
Next is the school song.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:26.800
Yamabuki High School

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:34.680
Oh no...

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:36.310
Ms. Yoshinoya...

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:44.030
I can run super fast!

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:50.200
But I'm so slow going this way.
I'm fast going this way.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:56.540
I'm so slow going this way,
but I'm so fast going this way.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:58.870
Miya, you'll upset the teachers.

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.580
Try it, Yunocchi!

00:06:08.010 --> 00:06:09.590
Miya...

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:11.300
I'm sorry.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:18.140
Not again.

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:21.980
Let's do at least the athlete's oath,
and call it a day.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:22.860
Miya?

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:24.480
Okay!

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:28.950
We swear, um...

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:31.070
Murmur...

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:33.450
Takeover sportsman ship...

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:34.580
Close, but incorrect!!!

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:38.370
I wonder if tomorrow will be fine?

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:47.510
Wow, my umbrella was almost
gonna turn inside out.

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:50.470
Miya, for some reason, you look happy.

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:53.850
Yeah, I get excited whenever a typhoon comes.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:57.600
I know. I get anxious too.

00:06:57.600 --> 00:06:58.100
<i>Hi</i>

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:58.600
<i>Da</i>

00:06:58.600 --> 00:06:59.100
<i>Ma</i>

00:06:59.100 --> 00:06:59.600
<i>Ri</i>

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:00.560
<i>Apartments</i>

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:11.030
Let's see how much water my bucket has.

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:13.820
Oh that's right, your place...

00:07:14.450 --> 00:07:15.780
What's wrong?

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:17.830
Now, I'm seriously nervous.

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:32.680
Don't you think the dripping pace is fast?

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:35.140
Probably because of the typhoon.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:51.280
What's that for?

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:55.280
As soon as the bucket is full,
we can switch right away.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:57.990
Yunocchi, good job.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:02.040
Let's keep some towels nearby,
in case the bucket is knocked over.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.420
Perfect!

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:15.930
Will these really catch fire when they get wet?

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:28.520
Hey, what are we going to do for supper?

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:30.400
Why don't we order a pizza?

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:33.610
Back at my parents place, we ordered
pizza every time a typhoon came.

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:36.490
Pizza...

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:52.090
How fast does a typhoon go?

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:54.260
Like 150 kilometers...

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:56.430
Per hour?

00:08:56.510 --> 00:09:01.560
I think it's even faster because it usually
passes by in three hours or so, doesn't it?

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:07.810
Which place is 100 km away from Kofu?

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:10.320
Well, let's see...

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:13.820
In the east, or the west?

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:16.860
What's the prefecture below Yamanashi?

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:18.490
Shizuoka.

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:21.120
Where's the weather channel?

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:25.250
I hope it passes soon.

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:28.580
Otherwise, tomorrow's event
will be canceled too.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:33.710
Why does a typhoon always come on the
day of school events or family trips?

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.840
Yunocchi, you must be a rain bringer.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:41.100
No, I can't be, although it happens
five times out of ten.

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:42.890
You are a rain bringer.

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:45.230
Is this all my fault?

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:49.730
Awesome, the storm-bringer girl!

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:52.020
I don't like that.

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:57.280
What are you talking about?

00:09:57.280 --> 00:09:59.860
We're just wondering where 100 km
away from Kofu is.

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:02.530
I wonder where...

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:09.080
By the way, east of Yamanashi is Tokyo and
Saitama. North and west is Nagano.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.170
What?

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:14.460
I'm thirsty.

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:16.670
I'd like to have some, too.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:26.020
You want some?

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:27.640
No, but thanks.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:30.980
I'll go make some tea.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:36.900
Hiro, stop. Don't move.

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:47.450
The power's flickering?

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:49.290
Time to dump the water.

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:53.290
Miya, be careful.

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:56.250
Seriously!

00:10:57.670 --> 00:11:03.800
I'm glad you worry about my place, but I
don't think you have to be that cautious.

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:08.390
If a fire breaks out, it'll be more
your place's problem.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:10.730
Well then, I have an idea.

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:13.770
All right everyone, move.

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:19.150
Did we get them all?

00:11:19.150 --> 00:11:24.070
Yup! I'll just have to take them somewhere,
and everyone will be safe.

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:25.450
You're right.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:27.490
Where are you going to take them to?

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.080
No idea.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:31.000
For now...

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:33.330
You hold them, Yunocchi.

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:37.050
Oh, c'mon.

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:40.220
It's Miya's fault, but Yuno,
you calm down, too.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:43.050
But I felt they were hot.

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:45.180
You're right. It's warm.

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:47.010
Are they wet?

00:11:47.260 --> 00:11:49.390
It'll catch fire after all.

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:50.720
Say...

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:54.900
The drying pouches are supposed to
catch fire when wet, right?

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:58.610
What will happen if we toss them into the rain?

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.610
They'll probably catch fire.

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:05.030
But it's raining outside. Would the fire last?

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:08.490
Let's try.

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:12.660
Miya, don't! It could be dangerous.

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:15.250
Here I go!

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:23.090
It didn't catch fire.

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:24.720
How disappointing.

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:31.310
Hey, Miyako, make sure you take
it to the trash. That's my yard.

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:44.900
I'll get going.

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:46.780
Already?

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:48.950
I'll go to Dada Mart.

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:50.540
To restock stuff?

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:52.160
You go all the way to Dada?

00:12:52.330 --> 00:12:57.040
It has to be a supermarket. Berry Mart
is a convenience store, after all.

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:59.670
We still don't know about tomorrow,

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:02.090
but I'll get some ingredients for
tomorrow's lunch just in case.

00:13:02.670 --> 00:13:04.550
Does it include ours by any chance?

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:07.760
I was going to make enough for four.

00:13:07.840 --> 00:13:09.470
Hurray!

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:18.900
Oh, I'll go with you. Since you're going to
cook, let me help you shop at least.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:20.730
Thank you.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:22.820
Yuno is so adorable.

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:24.610
Why don't you go, too?

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:35.460
I don't come here often.

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:38.750
It's a little far from the Hidamari Apartments.

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:41.880
The prices are cheaper than Berry Mart, though.

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:44.550
You're right.

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:50.220
What are you going to cook tomorrow?

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:53.060
Eat-up-to-beat-the-white-team lunch.

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:02.570
May I add these, too?

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:05.990
Go ahead...

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:07.820
Do you like these?

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:10.950
Yes, I'll go find more white stuff.

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:16.080
There's another white one,
but we don't need any more sugar.

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:20.880
Perhaps white drinks will work, too.

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:24.130
Here, these too.

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:30.840
Isn't gelatin transparent?

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:44.610
Are we buying snacks too?

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:46.480
It should be fine because
it's white chocolate.

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:49.070
I didn't say you can't.

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:53.200
There they are!

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:54.830
Hey!

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:56.330
Are you done?

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:58.450
Yeah, I browsed throughout the store.

00:14:58.450 --> 00:14:59.580
You just looked around?

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:00.920
Yup!

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:05.210
Total: 3,049 yen

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:05.210
(Tax: 145 yen)

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:04.420
The total comes to 3,049 yen.

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:06.050
Here you go.

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:08.720
Please draw a card from here.

00:15:10.510 --> 00:15:12.930
Um, you wanna try?

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:14.800
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes!

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:20.640
Blank?

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:22.350
Saury

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:22.350
It says saury.

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:26.570
We're back.

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:29.150
Welcome back. Good work.

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:31.490
Hey, check this out.

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:34.320
<i>Hi</i>

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:35.070
<i>Da</i>

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:35.780
<i>Ma</i>

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:36.530
<i>Ri</i>

00:15:36.530 --> 00:15:37.200
<i>Apartments</i>

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:39.250
Hi.

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:40.750
Hello.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.210
It's been a while.

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:45.790
Hello.

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:47.960
Yo.

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:49.800
What made you come here today?

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:53.970
Oh, a typhoon passed by, so I wanted
to check the apartments.

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:58.180
Why didn't you check when the
typhoon was approaching?

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:00.890
What's the point of checking
after it's almost passed?

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:04.270
Hell no. I don't wanna go outside
in the middle of the typhoon.

00:16:04.520 --> 00:16:06.270
Figures.

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:12.360
But I understand you. After all,
we also stayed inside.

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:14.280
See?

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:17.620
It's sunny above those clouds.

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:21.370
It must be beautiful above the clouds.

00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:25.750
Yeah, the open blue sky and endless clouds.

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:31.210
Sounds great. Don't you feel like you
could take a walk on the clouds?

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:33.300
I feel the same way.

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:35.510
I actually want to eat it.

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:37.510
I guess you could say that.

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:43.640
Stone-roasted sweet potatoes!

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:48.230
l wish I could take off, like ''zoom.''

00:16:48.230 --> 00:16:50.270
Sounds fun.

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:52.690
Excuse me.

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:57.620
I'm looking for the resident of Room 102?

00:16:57.820 --> 00:16:59.450
That's me.

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:03.660
It's from your mom.

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:05.370
It says fresh.

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:07.000
Let's see...

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:12.670
Wow!

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:19.890
This could be my first time seeing
chestnuts with the outside still intact.

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:21.970
Sae?

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:23.600
I know.

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:30.310
...coming?

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:36.400
It's nothing. I'm fine, I think.

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:40.990
Would you like some chestnut rice?

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:41.780
Sure!

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:44.870
But how are we going to crack the chestnuts?

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:46.500
Well...

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.710
Oh, I'll go get my bat.

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:51.420
I'm back.

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:53.420
Here you go, Sae. Try.

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:55.550
Do I have to do it?

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:58.840
Here comes my over-arm pitch.

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:00.680
Miya, time out!

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:03.140
Ah, chestnuts, huh? Looks good.

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:08.270
It's one of the popular autumn foods.
I haven't had any this year.

00:18:09.980 --> 00:18:12.270
Would you like to take this?

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:13.520
That's my...

00:18:13.520 --> 00:18:15.940
A saury? I can have this?

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:18.530
It's actually a prize. I hope you don't mind.

00:18:18.650 --> 00:18:21.320
Thank you. I'll grill it with some salt.

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:25.870
My prize...

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:29.460
Between chestnuts and saury,
I'll let her take a saury any day.

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:34.500
She knows what she wants. I couldn't
refuse because of the way she talked.

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:37.970
We all owe her to a certain extent.

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:40.430
Damn, that landlord!

00:18:43.550 --> 00:18:47.230
The landlord? Of Hidamari Apartments?

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:48.680
Yeah.

00:18:48.680 --> 00:18:51.810
I missed the chance to introduce myself.

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:56.280
You haven't met the landlord?

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:11.620
I'll go see the landlord tomorrow.

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:14.630
It's okay. Don't worry about it.

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:19.340
You'll be exhausted tomorrow. Once you get
home, you'll be too tired to get up.

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:22.470
Tomorrow is the sports festival.

00:19:22.470 --> 00:19:25.010
Oh, it stopped raining.

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:28.470
We've got to throw everything we've got.
We can't lose.

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:30.180
To the white team, right?

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:34.650
Right, she nags at me whenever she can.

00:19:35.060 --> 00:19:37.530
I don't want to hear her horse
laugh no matter what.

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:39.360
Oh, her.

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:46.700
Tonight, we eat good food, sleep well
and get ready for tomorrow.

00:19:46.780 --> 00:19:48.160
Okay.

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:49.830
Come to think of it...

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:56.210
What if the festival was canceled,
what would I do?

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:58.880
Should I prepare for the worst,
and not each too much today?

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:00.840
Don't worry, Hiro.

00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:04.550
Right, you didn't eat the saury after all.

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:07.720
But I ate a roasted sweet potato.

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:09.890
Hiro, stop slicing the chestnut.

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:24.200
Beauty

00:20:23.910 --> 00:20:26.030
Go red team.

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:26.030
Beauty

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:28.410
Um...

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:30.330
No, it's nothing.

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:32.910
What's so difficult to tell?

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:36.710
Well, I fell like I saw something else.

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:40.210
Even if it was what I saw,
we'll find out tomorrow anyway.

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:43.840
Let's do out best tomorrow.

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:45.470
Of course.

00:20:50.260 --> 00:20:51.930
Wow, it's done.

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:53.980
Looks tasty.

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:55.690
Here you go.

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:00.730
Smells good.

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:02.030
Well...

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:03.990
Thanks for the food.

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:09.700
Another one.

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:11.450
You still have some left in your bowl.

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:12.950
I'm reserving.

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:13.330
I do, too.

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:14.370
Me, too.
I do, too.

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:16.670
A reservation? Why don't you
finish yours first?

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:18.420
Then I make a reservation.

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:28.590
Twelve more hours to go?
l wonder if the ground will be dry?

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:33.770
I must not be a drag, but I feel pressured.

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:36.600
Would it be better if it's canceled?

00:21:37.270 --> 00:21:41.770
No, I can't be a wimp.
Everyone's going to do their best.

00:21:44.820 --> 00:21:46.400
So cold!

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:54.540
Tomorrow will be sunny for sure.

00:21:55.330 --> 00:21:56.960
Yunocchi!

00:21:57.460 --> 00:21:59.540
The moon! It looks like a chestnut.

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:02.920
Yup!

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:05.840
The end of October 12th

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:05.840
To Be Continued

00:22:05.880 --> 00:22:08.800
Good luck with the sports festival!

00:22:14.060 --> 00:22:21.480
It eventually fades into the tall sky

00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:23.110
The voices

00:22:23.820 --> 00:22:27.900
Bubble up and fade away

00:22:28.860 --> 00:22:31.320
Fade away

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:36.000
They return to where they belong

00:22:37.330 --> 00:22:44.500
And fuse together as they sparkle and collide

00:22:46.380 --> 00:22:50.010
This body feels like one entity

00:22:50.010 --> 00:22:53.180
Yet, it's made of infinity

00:22:53.180 --> 00:22:56.560
Caught a falling drop of water

00:22:56.560 --> 00:23:02.560
And now I'm taking a closer look

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:05.230
Awakening Drive

00:23:05.230 --> 00:23:09.650
Dash into the sky in our bare feet

00:23:09.650 --> 00:23:13.870
Close your eyes, can you see it?

00:23:13.870 --> 00:23:17.040
It's a rainbow bridge, let's run toward it

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:18.700
Awakening Drive

00:23:18.700 --> 00:23:23.080
A dazzling spark will break a star into pieces

00:23:23.080 --> 00:23:31.260
Scattering across the sky and falling,
now in my hands

00:23:31.630 --> 00:23:37.890
l have a piece of a dream, shining so bright

00:23:39.810 --> 00:23:42.100
What happened to Sae?

00:23:42.100 --> 00:23:45.650
She doesn't respond to the
door bell or my knock.

00:23:45.980 --> 00:23:49.440
There's a flavorful aroma
coming from Hiro's place.

00:23:49.530 --> 00:23:52.990
Plus, she carries food cautiously as
if she doesn't want to be found.

00:23:53.280 --> 00:23:54.820
Could it be...

00:23:54.820 --> 00:23:57.450
She's hiding from her debt collector?!

00:23:57.990 --> 00:24:02.460
Next Episode is
''March 13th: 3% of Hope''

00:24:02.460 --> 00:24:06.460
We'll be waiting at the Hidamari Apartments,
so please, join us again.
